  "prep_topics": [
    "Networking: TCP vs UDP, and the TCP 3-way handshake",
    "Networking: what happens when you type a URL (DNS, TCP, TLS, HTTP)",
    "Networking: the TLS handshake and certificates",
    "Reliability: timeouts, retries with exponential backoff, idempotency",
    "Go: context for cancellation and deadlines (read job-radar internal/source/source.go)",
    "Go: goroutines, channels, select, and a worker pool (read job-radar main.go scan())",
    "Go: Mutex vs RWMutex vs channels, and go test -race",
    "Go: interfaces and error handling (wrapping, errors.Is / errors.As)",
    "Go: table-driven tests, httptest, mocks",
    "FitDuel story: the WebSocket slow-client fix, out loud in 30 seconds",
    "FitDuel story: ~250 queries to 2 (N+1), out loud in 30 seconds",
    "SQL: joins and GROUP BY (interview-playground/sql/02, 03)",
    "SQL: indexes and EXPLAIN (interview-playground/sql/07)",
    "SQL: transactions, isolation levels, locking (interview-playground/sql/06)",
    "Redis: data types, sorted-set leaderboards, Pub/Sub",
    "API design: status codes, pagination, versioning, auth",
    "Queues: SQS, dead-letter queues, at-least-once delivery, idempotent consumers",
    "DSA: arrays and hashing (2 LeetCode easy)",
    "DSA: two pointers and sliding window (2 problems)",
    "DSA: stacks and queues (2 problems)",
    "DSA: binary search (2 problems)",
    "DSA: trees, BFS and DFS (2 problems)",
    "DSA: graphs (1-2 problems)",
    "System design: URL shortener (explain Snippy end to end)",
    "System design: rate limiter",
    "Docker: images, layers, multi-stage builds",
    "OS basics: process vs thread, how the Go scheduler runs goroutines",
    "Behavioral: tell me about yourself + why are you switching (2 minutes, out loud)"
  ]
}
